WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our first guest tonight
is a talented actor

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:02.836 line:92%
you know best as Sam Wilso

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:05.538
from the "Captain America"
and "Avengers" franchise,

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:06.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
as well as
the critically acclaimed

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:10.243
Disney+ series "The Falcon
and the Winter Soldier."

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:11.745 line:92%
He can be seen next in "Solos,

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:15.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
which appears on
Amazon Prime Video on May 21st

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:17.083 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's wrong.
-What?

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:21.755 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-What? Really, what?

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:24.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look, everything, alright?
Everything is wrong.

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:27.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I read that every reunion
is different.

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:27.761 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Don't call it that.

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:28.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What do you want me
to call it, Tom?

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:31.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know,
but it's not a reunion.

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hmm.
-I shouldn't have called.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:35.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
Alright?
I should have never called

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:36.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I wouldn't be here
if you hadn't called.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:40.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's what I'm saying.
My nose isn't...

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.942 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Uh, I have a...

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:47.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
And your neck, it's all, like,
[Bleep ] necky.

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:48.848 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-We're identical, Tom.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:53.953
You think this is easy for m
to meet you for the first time

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:56.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, [Bleep] it must be
easy for you.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:57.424 line:92%
If you think you look like me,

00:00:57.424 --> 00:01:00.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
it must be like
winning a [Bleep] jackpot.

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:02.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome back
to the show Anthony Mackie

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:04.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
How are you, Anthony?
-[ Chuckles ]

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
What's up, my man.
How is it going?

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:08.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm doing well.
So, we both have young kids.

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:09.436 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And, look, I get it.

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:11.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
My kids aren't gonna
want to watch a show like this

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:15.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I assume --
you're in the superhero game -

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:20.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
that your kids would go craz
to watch your work.

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
And yet they're
not into the Marvel stuff.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Chuckles ]
No, not at all.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:28.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're a board-game family,
so I had to force them

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:31.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
to watch "The Falcon
and the Winter Soldier,"

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:34.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it's World War III
over here

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.095 line:92%
when we play our board games

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:38.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've ripped up
many a Hungry Hungry Hippo

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:41.267 line:92%
going at it over board games

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.268 size:84% position:42% line:92%
But they got to see it.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hungry Hungry Hippos,
I'm just gonna say,

00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:46.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
my wife's all-time
least-favorite game.

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:49.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, marbles everywhere.
It's just a mess.

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:51.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a mess.
-She despises all those hippos

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:54.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it's even worse
when you have to

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
continuously fix the hippos.
-Yeah.

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:58.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then the dog
gets the hippos,

00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:01.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
the dog chews the hippos,
you have to order a new one.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.155 size:81% position:41% line:92%
It's always a problem.

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:04.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I will say,
for as much as we play it,

00:02:04.324 --> 00:02:05.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
when one of the hippos
gets broke,

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:08.194
I thought, at this point, it
would be better fixing them.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:11.197
And every time, I feel lik
I'm starting at square one

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:14.434 line:92%
-[ Laughs ] It's impossible.

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:15.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have Sebastian Stan
on the show,

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:20.006
and he said that neither of yo
really knew the extent to whic

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:22.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Falcon and
the Winter Soldier"

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:24.244
was going to be a series,
but you ran into each othe

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:26.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the same hotel,
and based on that,

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:29.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
started to piece it together
-Yeah, we were --

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:33.153
And I had no idea where he was
because he lives in New York

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:36.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
I live in New Orleans.
So, I come down to the lobby

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:38.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I see him in the lobby
and I'm like, "Uh,

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:40.660
what are you doing here?"
He's like, "You have a meeting?"

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:41.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "Yeah.
You have a meeting?"

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:45.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like, "Yeah."
Like, "Ah, you're gonna do it?

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "I don't know."
[ Laughs ]

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:51.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was, like, this amazing
Texas standoff

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.038 size:84% position:42% line:92%
for about five minutes.

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:54.574 size:81% position:41%
Then, we stood outside
waiting for our cars,

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:55.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
and neither one of us
said anything.

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:58.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Alright,
see you after your meeting."

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:01.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like, "Yeah, you too.
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:04.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know it's pointless to tr
to get any information

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:08.021
about "Captain America 4,"
which was just announced.

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:10.557 line:92%
But this is interesting to me.

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:11.758 line:92%
I assume someone like you

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:14.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
would find out
via some secret back channel

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:16.696 size:84% position:42%
but you were actually
just in the supermarket

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:19.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you got word.
-Well, that's the funny thing.

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:23.269
I thought, being upgraded
to the suit and the shield

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:25.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would be the first guy
to get information,

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, get a phone call
"Hey, Anthony.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is what we're thinking.
What do you think?"

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:32.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I was literally --
When I go to the grocery store

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:35.248
I have my same guy that I go to,
and I've known him forever

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:38.117
And he'll close his line
until I get to the front.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:39.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just, like, go through
right?

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:43.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I go up, and he's like
"Yo, is this real?"

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:47.760
And he had the announcemen
about "Cap 4" on his phone

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I still haven't heard
anything from Marvel.

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:54.100
I have no idea what's happening.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:57.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
-As long as I know
I'm not fired, I'm happy.

00:03:57.704 --> 00:03:59.105 line:92%
-That was a clip we showed

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:02.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
from your new anthology
series, "Solos."

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:06.679
This obviously seems like
a nice change in tempo,

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:07.447 size:84% position:42% line:92%
change in pace for you.

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:10.783 size:88% position:44%
And it's sort of been --
being an anthology show,

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:13.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
it must feel a little bit more
like your theater roots

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:15.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
than playing the same characte
over a series of films.

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:19.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, 100%, and
that's why I wanted to do it

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:21.761 line:92%
This whole piece, "Solo," is

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:24.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Helen Mirren
and Morgan Freeman,

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:26.833 line:92%
it's just such an amazing cast

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.534 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Nicole Beharie.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.069 line:92%
And to get the opportunity

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:32.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
to play yourself
against yourself

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:36.142
is something a lot of actors
don't get the opportunity to do.

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:39.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's such
an amazingly dramatic

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:41.114 size:88% position:44% line:92%
but humbling experience.

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:43.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I was excited
to be a part of it,

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:44.917 line:92%
'cause it was like doing a play.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:48.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was 35 pages
of me running my mouth.

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:50.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, it was --
It was an experience.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:53.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How did you enjoy
working with Anthony Mackie?

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:56.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
How was he --
-You know what? You know what?

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:59.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I know why people
like me so much now.

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:03.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm a pretty dope dude.
[ Both laughs ]

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:05.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Show up on time,
know your lines.

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:07.240
That's what everybody says
-Know your lines, everything

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not -- I always brough
myself something back

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:13.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
from craft service.
I gave myself notes on stuff

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:15.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was great, man.
I would do every movie with me

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:19.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I hope you know
I'm not just blowing smoke

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:22.355
You guys have amazing chemistry.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:25.958
-The two Anthony Mackies,
just absolutely amazing.

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:27.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, we had
a great time together.

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:29.228 size:75% position:38%
There's nothing like
answering yourself

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:30.763
when you're talking to yourself.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:33.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You -- I read -- And again,
like I said,

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:36.636
I know you have a background -
a theater school background,

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:40.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you will still go bac
and read Shakespeare

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:46.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
for pleasure and relaxation.
-Yeah, that's my thing.

00:05:46.212 --> 00:05:49.515 line:92%
You know, with good jobs,

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:52.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
you get gifts from
your agents and managers.

00:05:52.185 --> 00:05:55.054 size:81% position:41%
So, you know, I got,
like, the first folio.

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.456 line:92%
I got the original edition

00:05:56.456 --> 00:05:57.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got all these
different editions.

00:05:57.724 --> 00:06:01.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, it's interesting to see,
you know, the difference

00:06:01.461 --> 00:06:03.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
every time a new edition
came out

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:05.164 line:92%
and how those words would change

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:06.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
the meaning of
a monologue or a play.

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:09.836 size:81% position:41%
So, I always go back
just to keep up on it,

00:06:09.836 --> 00:06:11.170 size:78% position:39% line:92%
'cause you never know

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:13.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you're gonna get
that phone call.

00:06:13.606 --> 00:06:15.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
"Shakespeare in the Park, man.

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:19.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got to prepare --
That's a lifelong preparation.

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:20.413 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know?

00:06:20.413 --> 00:06:21.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm heartbroken
to tell you this.

00:06:21.581 --> 00:06:25.418
The other Anthony Mackie got it.
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:27.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, to be
a true New York actor,

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:28.921 line:92%
you have to do "Law &amp; Order"

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:30.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you have to do
Shakespeare in the Park.

00:06:30.957 --> 00:06:32.125 line:92%
That's the two requirements.

00:06:32.125 --> 00:06:33.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If you can tick
those two boxes.

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:36.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
How young were you
the first time you Shakespeare

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:39.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The first time
I did Shakespeare,

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:42.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was in ninth grade,
so I was 14.

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:45.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was 14 years old.
My teacher, Ray Frizell,

00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:47.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
gave me a play to read,
and I was --

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:50.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
I went to public school
in New Orleans at the time

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:52.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
when New Orleans was
the worse place on Earth.

00:06:52.445 --> 00:06:56.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
The teachers were more about
keeping kids in school

00:06:56.015 --> 00:06:58.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
than introducing them to stuff
And this one teacher

00:06:58.718 --> 00:07:01.854
really just opened my eyes
to the world of literature

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:03.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
and introduced me
to Ibsen and Chekhov

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:08.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
and all these different
aspects of culture

00:07:08.494 --> 00:07:09.662 line:92%
that I had never heard of.

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:11.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Shakespeare --
I was blown away

00:07:11.597 --> 00:07:13.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
that this white dude
500 years ago

00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:15.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
could write a play
that I could relate to today

00:07:15.468 --> 00:07:17.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You mentioned
you were in New Orleans.

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:20.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we have talked about
being NFL fans

00:07:20.006 --> 00:07:22.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
in some of your recent visits.
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:22.909 --> 00:07:25.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you -- I mean, I gues
one of the downsides

00:07:25.445 --> 00:07:28.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
of being a Saints fan is,
they're so good

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:30.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they never really hav
a particularly high draft pick

00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:34.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
But did you enjoy their draft,
as it were?

00:07:34.086 --> 00:07:36.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know what?
I will say --

00:07:36.489 --> 00:07:39.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I give --
If nothing else fails,

00:07:39.158 --> 00:07:42.962
we have the smartest draft
selections out of everybody.

00:07:42.962 --> 00:07:45.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
If they just rate everybod
on their GPAs,

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:47.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
we literally broke the --
we have --

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:49.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
we drafted
a whole team of accountants.

00:07:49.969 --> 00:07:51.637 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:55.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm very happy about the dudes
that we drafted.

00:07:55.041 --> 00:07:56.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have a damn good lineup
this year.

00:07:56.609 --> 00:07:59.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's good.
I wish you the best of luck.

00:07:59.011 --> 00:08:01.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here, Anthony.

00:08:01.214 --> 00:08:03.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
And congrats on everything
-Thanks a lot.

00:08:03.783 --> 00:08:05.618 size:81% position:41%
Good to see you, man.
-Good to see you, too.

00:08:05.618 --> 00:08:07.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Solos" premieres
on Amazon Prime Video

00:08:07.854 --> 00:08:10.022 size:75% position:38% line:92%
on Friday, May 21st.

